  "goodToKnow": "Sprießen means to sprout or shoot up: Die Knospen sprießen, Sein Bart sprießt. Figuratively, things sprießen wie Pilze aus dem Boden (spring up like mushrooms), such as new shops or start-ups. It's irregular and takes sein: spross, ist gesprossen. Der Spross is a shoot, and humorously an offspring; die Sprossen are sprouts and also the rungs of a ladder."
